1
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:03,960
The Bauer Kingdom,

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:07,986
bordered on the west by Sus and
on the east by the Noor Empire,

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:10,219
which remains a threat to this day.

4
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:15,597
Powerful families within the kingdom's
bounds rose to prominence over the years.

5
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:18,000
They became today's royals and nobles,

6
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,224
taxing commoners in their
bid to maintain peace.

7
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:26,864
However, the rise of magic blurred divisions
of power, threatening the status quo.

8
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:29,980
Because King LaSalle
believes in meritocracy,

9
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:34,184
he began admitting commoners to
the Royal Academy on scholarship.

10
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:38,320
Everyone would be treated
equally, or so he thought.

11
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:00,500
No, I'm not afraid of
What you want to say now?

12
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:14,980
Happy end You don't know Your love

13
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:22,080
Your love Your love Hey!

14
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:27,897
I can't believe it,
you're happy to be here!

15
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:28,810
You can't believe it,
you're happy to be here!

16
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:43,880
You can't believe it,
let's just accept it!

17
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:45,250
And after that, the world is happy.

18
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:46,163
It's weep and our eyes.

19
00:01:46,246 --> 00:01:48,497
You can't believe it,
we might not believe it?

20
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:49,410
But if we're happy when we've been back,

21
00:01:49,493 --> 00:01:51,754
We should love it, the heart is coming.

22
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:58,477
Thank you.

23
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:01,757
I don't want to give up
until I think I don't want

24
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,977
to give up until I think
I don't want to give up

25
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:06,680
It's a fun game, I love you!

26
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:32,337
I don't know exactly what
happened, but no one deserves that.

27
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:36,655
Most likely the commoner said something
offensive to provoke the attack.

28
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:39,097
They're a little faction.

29
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:41,768
It's called the commoner
movement, isn't it?

30
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:45,917
They were spewing nonsense about
nobles and commoners being equal.

31
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,941
Foolish claims with no basis in
reality, and look what they led to.

32
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:53,297
It's no wonder they say the
tongue is the whip of evil.

33
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:58,320
You say that, but what would you think
if a noble spoke out and got hurt?

34
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,150
A...

35
00:03:00,233 --> 00:03:01,063
a noble?

36
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,657
Hypothetically, of course.

37
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:07,093
But non-hypothetically.

38
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,122
You can whip me evilly any time.

39
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:14,780
This is the only reality she knows.

40
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,729
Guess I can't blame
her for not getting it.

41
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:20,860
Um, pardon me.

42
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,845
We've completed his treatment.

43
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,350
Hello again.

44
00:03:33,433 --> 00:03:34,263
Matt, right?

45
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:36,990
Taylor?

46
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,537
I hate to do this to you
while you're recovering,

47
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:41,937
but the Academy Knights
have some questions.

48
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:46,138
I'm sure you must be in pain, but
do you think you could answer a few?

49
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:48,530
I refuse.

50
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:53,437
Everyone knows the knights are
those disgusting nobles' lapdogs,

51
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:56,437
and I have absolutely
nothing to say to a commoner

52
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:59,167
who pledges her loyalty
to the likes of them.

53
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:00,420
Listen, Matt.

54
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:03,307
The knights are here to
protect all students.

55
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,620
And, well, cooperating would be wise.

56
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,160
We're commoners just like you.

57
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:12,877
We know how hard it is to redeem
yourself after crossing a noble.

58
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:13,837
And why is that?

59
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,237
Why is it a risk for us
to voice our opinions?

60
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:18,026
This is why we need to fight!

61
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,120
Try to relax, okay?

62
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:25,377
We're here to get your side of the story
and make sure you're treated fairly.

63
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:28,989
So please, Matt, just tell me
what happened out there today.

64
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:33,320
It started when me and some
others approached Prince Yu.

65
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:37,089
He honestly listened
to what we had to say.

66
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:40,195
But then that jerk found out about it.

67
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:44,720
You there, commoner,
stay away from Prince Yu!

68
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:48,320
I was livid, and I couldn't help myself.

69
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:51,240
I told them what I really thought.

70
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:55,177
I said that royals and nobles were
nothing but tax-leeching parasites.

71
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:56,554
What did you just say?

72
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,877
Please just stay calm, Miss Claire.

73
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:01,725
It's important that we
hear what he has to say.

74
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,560
It wasn't about me.

75
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:08,512
I couldn't stand him speaking out of you.

76
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:12,737
So, without even thinking, I took
out my wand to defend your honor.

77
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:13,960
What did you say?

78
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:18,360
Insolent mongrel, you shut your
mouth or I'll shut it for you!

79
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:29,266
And the next thing I
knew I was waking up here

80
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:37,577
Damn it who do these nobles
think they are one of them burned

81
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:41,366
me alive because I took a stand
on something he disagreed with.

82
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,420
I was just trying to scare him.

83
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:49,040
I had no intention of using magic.

84
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:51,080
I didn't mean to hurt him.

85
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,220
I swear in the name of God.

86
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,060
His wand, where is it?

87
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:58,634
It's already been confiscated
and sent off for analysis.

88
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:01,002
I'll also be inspecting it soon.

89
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:05,000
That innocent boy could
have been any one of us.

90
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:07,057
We won't stand for this oppression.

91
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:09,434
We will continue to fight for equality.

92
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:12,718
We demand justice for our
brother and safety for all!

93
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:17,380
Word travels fast.

94
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,417
Even people who don't go to
school here are up in arms.

95
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:21,330
Hey, you.

96
00:06:21,413 --> 00:06:24,917
Mind explaining to us what you were doing
with this Matt guy in the first place?

97
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,757
He wanted to speak to me
about his group's objective.

98
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:30,057
He asked me to listen,
which was only fair,

99
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:32,317
but I never agreed to support their cause.

100
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:35,988
Whether you did or not, that
was a pretty careless move, you.

101
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:39,100
You need to consider your
position in this kingdom.

102
00:06:40,780 --> 00:06:43,540
Before God, all are
equal, so we are taught.

103
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:46,271
A tenet of the spiritual church, I assume?

104
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:49,820
The church opens its doors
to anyone who knocks.

105
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:54,397
It would have been wrong of me to turn
that boy away without hearing him out.

106
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:58,957
On the subject of the church, let's talk
about the lineage of the Bauer family.

107
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:03,417
Prince Rod and Prince Thane are the sons
of a princess from the land of the Alps.

108
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:06,460
She was the former queen
and died at a young age.

109
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:10,240
Prince Yu's mother, Grishe,
is the current queen.

110
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:14,197
Before she married the king, she was
a cardinal of the spiritual church,

111
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:15,937
hence her son's scripture reciting.

112
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:17,977
The church is the dominant religion here,

113
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,277
and it centers around
devotion to the spirits.

114
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:23,717
The kingdom hoped that the marriage
would give it power over the church,

115
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,017
but that didn't happen.

116
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:25,930
Instead,

117
00:07:26,013 --> 00:07:29,697
the church grew even more powerful thanks
to its connection to the royal family.

118
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:34,377
Prince Yu is often seen as a symbol of
the church's authority over the kingdom.

119
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:35,290
Ahem.

120
00:07:35,373 --> 00:07:39,297
The teachings of the Church tend to align
most with the commoner movement's beliefs.

121
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:43,674
I've even heard rumors floating around
that the Church is financing them.

122
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:48,765
My guess is Matt and his friends approached
Prince Yu in hopes of requesting aid.

123
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,577
I'll admit that meeting
with them was irresponsible,

124
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:55,037
but Deed would never
hurt anyone on purpose!

125
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,580
I'd stake my life on it!

126
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,277
Apparently Deed's defense
is that he lost control

127
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:03,184
of his wand and the magic
discharged on its own.

128
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:05,379
Were any defects found in the wand?

129
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:09,557
I personally examined it
while keeping that in mind,

130
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,877
but I saw no signs that
it had malfunctioned.

131
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:16,254
If someone who knows magic tools as
well as you says so, it must be true.

132
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:21,197
Honestly, whatever occurs outside
the academy is beyond our control.

133
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:25,057
Let's stay focused on what we can
do until Deed's fate is determined.

134
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:27,557
The three of us can chat
with the noble students.

135
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:29,717
Hopefully something will get through.

136
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:32,017
Rey and Misha, you handle the commoners.

137
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:34,957
Listen to their grievances
and try to calm things down.

138
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:37,437
You don't seem too pleased
to have been given that task.

139
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:38,350
Cause I'm not.

140
00:08:38,433 --> 00:08:41,812
I suck at talking to people
about serious stuff like this.

141
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:45,097
Although a head pat from you
might make me feel better.

142
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:46,010
A what?

143
00:08:46,093 --> 00:08:47,705
You want me to do my best try.

144
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:49,680
Do it, Claire.

145
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:56,757
You can do it, I believe in you.

146
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,977
Could you add a pinch of
love, like a tiny piece?

147
00:08:59,060 --> 00:08:59,942
No, Miss Queen!

148
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:00,990
No snaps!

149
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:04,049
Let's get to work, people.

150
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:08,160
We've got a campus to quiet down,
and not much time to do it. Yeah!

151
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:29,180
It's too crowded in here of course.

152
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:31,437
It's crowded the sentence
is about to be posted.

153
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,520
We all want to know what'll happen

154
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,320
There he is.

155
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:45,700
What no that can't be right!

156
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:51,300
Dean Murray is sentenced to be
under house arrest for one week.

157
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,777
I just killed someone!

158
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,566
What kind of justice is that?

159
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:00,710
Miss Claire!

160
00:10:02,420 --> 00:10:04,157
Nobles shouldn't be here right now.

161
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,070
But why?

162
00:10:05,153 --> 00:10:07,777
Someone has to calm this
chaos, but where are we going?

163
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:08,919
Quickly, this way.

164
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:12,460
It keeps getting worse.

165
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:14,348
What's going to happen now?

166
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:18,160
What happened to your meritocracy?

167
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:20,997
Isn't everyone supposed to
be equal at the Academy?

168
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:23,337
Nothing has changed and nothing ever will.

169
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:25,714
The Nobles will always come out on top.

170
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:31,636
Entry into the academy is prohibited!

171
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:33,095
Get back, all of you!

172
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:37,651
The academy will be on temporary lockdown,

173
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:41,768
and the military will join our
guards until the protests end.

174
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:44,180
I will not stay quiet about this.

175
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:45,660
It's not enough.

176
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:47,797
That boy can't stand up to walk.

177
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:51,440
And yet, his attacker's
punishment is to stay at home?

178
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:54,661
Trust me, everyone here
feels the same way you do.

179
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,717
But it appears that some nobles
who disagree with the commoner

180
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:01,177
movement sought a reduced sentence
and got what they requested.

181
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:03,789
I thought they'd been
awfully quiet lately.

182
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:07,320
We let this happen right
under our noses. There's more.

183
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:10,217
Turns out the church is giving
its support to the nobles.

184
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:12,077
But that doesn't make any sense.

185
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:15,337
The church has been financing the
commoner movement, haven't they?

186
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:17,257
That's a political move, I'm sure.

187
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:21,417
They may claim that they never get involved
in politics, but that's obviously a lie.

188
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:22,971
Power struggles as usual.

189
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:26,477
They want to take public
support from the royal family.

190
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:29,617
They help both commoners and
nobles in order to heighten the

191
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:33,288
tension between them and weaken
the authority of the kingdom.

192
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:41,640
You, does Queen Rishay know about this?

193
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:42,820
Who can say?

194
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:46,258
I am not privy to my mother's
thoughts on the matter.

195
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:47,210
Why not?

196
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:49,037
Can't you just go talk to her?

197
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:51,237
I requested a meeting, but she refused.

198
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:53,438
I suppose that's her right as queen.

199
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:57,168
Yes, but she's your
mother first, isn't she?

200
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:59,465
What exactly are you implying?

201
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:01,240
It was a simple question.

202
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:04,380
Being her son does not
give me any power in this.

203
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,070
Pardon me.

204
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:10,900
I wonder if this is what
the church is truly after.

205
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,122
Think about it.

206
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:15,769
Perhaps they're trying to create
a rift between the princes.

207
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:18,577
Perhaps so.

208
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:21,601
Having us at odds would
undermine royal authority.

209
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:24,277
I think you may be onto something, Claire.

210
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:27,577
Fortunately, the military will be
protecting us from outside the gate.

211
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:31,778
But it's our job as knights to protect
the school grounds from within.

212
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:52,490
Miss Claire?

213
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:55,200
Yes? What is it?

214
00:12:55,960 --> 00:13:00,901
Once you make it back to your room, I need
you to stay there until tomorrow morning.

215
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:02,210
What?

216
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:05,377
How can you ask something like that
with everything that's happening?

217
00:13:05,460 --> 00:13:09,497
It's the Academy Knight's job to be
on call at a time like this, isn't it?

218
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,737
So you're saying you won't do as I ask?

219
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:12,980
Of course I won't.

220
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:16,340
I understand.

221
00:13:17,060 --> 00:13:18,707
Then you leave me no choice.

222
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:23,360
Miss Claire!

223
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:26,729
What have you done to her?

224
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:27,730
It's alright.

225
00:13:27,813 --> 00:13:29,839
I just put her to sleep with magic.

226
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:34,825
Now please, escort her to the
dorm and hide there until morning.

227
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:38,594
Promise you won't leave the
room no matter what happens.

228
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:42,274
Tonight, the protesters will
break down the school gate.

229
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:43,870
What?

230
00:13:43,953 --> 00:13:45,918
Wait, you know something, don't you?

231
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:47,600
Tell me what's going on.

232
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:50,920
Lene, you love Miss Claire, right?

233
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,077
Why would you ever doubt that?

234
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:56,395
I've been in her service for
much longer than you have!

235
00:13:58,300 --> 00:13:59,130
Good.

236
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:00,408
Then I'll leave her to you.

237
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,894
I'm trusting you to do the right thing.

238
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:09,020
Rey, wait!

239
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:31,100
The soldiers just went down.

240
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:34,285
Not sure what happened,
but this is our chance.

241
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:43,486
Captain, the protesters
have reached the gate.

242
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:46,517
Cooperate with the military
and try to quiet the mob.

243
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:49,365
We must protect the
Academy no matter the cost.

244
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:50,980
Where are the doors?

245
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:53,877
That noble is gonna get
what's coming to him!

246
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,960
Stop right there! Huh?

247
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:59,014
This is an order from your future king!

248
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:01,600
Do not take a single step closer!

249
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:19,397
What you're wasting time
I destroyed that bell

250
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:22,680
of yours now you have no
way to control monsters?

251
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:29,620
It was a clever invention but
you'll never get to use it!

252
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:31,780
Master Lambert

253
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:43,020
Hold on, right? Taylor?

254
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:44,417
How did...

255
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:46,000
what are you doing here?

256
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:47,697
Stopping you before it's too late.

257
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,837
I think you might be confused.

258
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:53,597
I was told about the riot and came here
to protect these priceless magic tools.

259
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:54,957
You can drop the act now!

260
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,864
What did you do to Deed's wand?

261
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,537
What are you talking about?

262
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:01,560
His wand was fine. I checked.

263
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:03,309
And everyone believed you.

264
00:16:04,020 --> 00:16:06,340
Because you're a magic tool specialist.

265
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:09,739
It's your job to inspect
and maintain all the tools.

266
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:13,657
So it'd be pretty easy for you to rig
Deed's wand to discharge on its own.

267
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:16,034
And to eliminate evidence of tampering.

268
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:17,535
Child's play, really.

269
00:16:18,740 --> 00:16:20,681
And it wasn't just that incident.

270
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:25,900
You've been encouraging animosity between
nobles and commoners this whole time.

271
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:29,057
Once the rioters overran the school,

272
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:32,517
You were planning to ring that
bell and make monsters attack.

273
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,430
Am I right?

274
00:16:33,513 --> 00:16:34,440
Or am I right?

275
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,220
Well, that's a fascinating hypothesis.

276
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:40,874
But do you have evidence to back it up?

277
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:42,260
No, none at all.

278
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:46,900
But proof or not, I know everything.

279
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:51,160
For example, I know the commoner
movement means nothing to you.

280
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:54,997
Let's assume what you're
saying is correct.

281
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:58,040
What sort of motive would
I have to do any of it?

282
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:00,300
He has a point.

283
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:03,917
The kingdom relies on
the Oruso Company for

284
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,277
the mining and distribution
of magic stones,

285
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:09,125
and they've accumulated
massive wealth from it.

286
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:13,017
If they were to dismantle the
system that gave them their riches,

287
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:14,747
they'd be left with nothing.

288
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:17,900
There's only one reason
he'd take such a risk.

289
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:21,385
They're using Lene as
a hostage, aren't they?

290
00:17:23,020 --> 00:17:24,660
I know about that, too.

291
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:27,421
She's more than just your sister.

292
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:29,801
She's someone you love very much.

293
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,380
What does that mean?

294
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:34,940
Ray Taylor, tell me what you know.

295
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:38,797
Can you believe that some would say
homosexuality is the forbidden love?

296
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:42,117
But here you are with Lene, and
she's your blood sibling, and you...

297
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,030
Stop it!

298
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:46,120
Don't say another word!

299
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,460
Please, Ray!

300
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:50,500
Just stop! Lene, don't.

301
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,200
Don't do it!

302
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:55,197
Promise you won't get in my brother's way!

303
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:56,397
I don't...

304
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:58,020
I don't want to hurt Ms.

305
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,340
Claire, but I will!

306
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:03,940
It's such a shame, Lene.

307
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:08,060
Master Lambert, please stop this.

308
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:11,280
I promise you I'll do
something to help Lene.

309
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:12,920
You can.

310
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,060
Master Lambert!

311
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,897
You don't know how terrifying he is.

312
00:18:15,980 --> 00:18:19,451
If I fail, you'll kill Lene
without a moment's hesitation.

313
00:18:19,620 --> 00:18:20,640
I mean it, Ray!

314
00:18:24,980 --> 00:18:27,260
I just can't sleep in peace, can I?

315
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:29,410
Miss Claire!

316
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,190
Lene?

317
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:39,000
I'm sure I don't know the full
story here, but tell me...

318
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:42,932
Is it accurate to say that you
two are behind all of this?

319
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:45,057
Surrender now while you have the chance!

320
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:48,577
I don't care what you were planning
to do, this is where it ends!

321
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:49,680
Is it now?

322
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:54,140
I'm afraid that won't do it all.

323
00:18:56,280 --> 00:19:00,100
Whatever's going on right now,
it isn't a plotline in the game.

324
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,660
I don't recognize any of this.

325
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:04,340
Who is he?

326
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:08,940
Now, Lambert, be a good
boy and call the monster.

327
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:10,960
The bell is broken.

328
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:12,460
Not a problem.

329
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,960
All better now.

330
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:20,797
As long as you hold up
your end of the bargain,

331
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:23,637
I'll help you escape the
country as I promised.

332
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:27,544
Then you and your sister can live
a new life with new identities.

333
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:31,488
You two could finally have the
life you've always dreamed of.

334
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:32,760
Go on.

335
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:36,150
Lambert, wait!

336
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,837
You don't have to do this!

337
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:39,861
You want that freedom, don't you?

338
00:19:40,020 --> 00:19:43,255
What would it be like not to
hide your love any longer?

339
00:19:45,900 --> 00:19:47,640
I'm sorry, Miss Claire.

340
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,099
Please forgive me.

341
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:50,780
But it's too late.

342
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,800
We can't go back now!

343
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:14,520
Is that a Chimera? I'm waiting.

344
00:20:16,660 --> 00:20:19,840
Chimera, I command you
to eliminate the nobles!

345
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:27,717
Come on, Miss Claire.

346
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:28,682
We need backup.

347
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:30,511
Let's go find the guards.

348
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:31,890
No.

349
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,440
What do you mean, no?

350
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:38,884
Retreating may mean more casualties and
harsher punishment for Lene and Lambert.

351
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:41,062
We'll just have to hold it here.

352
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:42,987
Lene is my responsibility.

353
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:45,360
She belongs to me!

354
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:52,579
Responsibility, let's call it that.

355
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,153
You're such a tsundere!

356
00:20:55,740 --> 00:20:58,387
What on earth is a
tsundere and why am I one?

357
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:00,257
We're at a disadvantage in here.

358
00:21:00,340 --> 00:21:01,597
We need to go somewhere else.

359
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,445
You just blatantly ignored me!

360
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:06,150
Miss Claire!

361
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:07,570
Miss Claire!

362
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:20,948
And she sticks the landing!

363
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:36,080
Sub-Zero-free!

364
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:47,117
Those magic skills of yours
are completely ridiculous.

365
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:50,797
There's no magic too ridiculous
for a lady ridiculously in love.

366
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:51,710
Really? Now?

367
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:58,080
It possesses multiple
attributes, a head of fire,

368
00:21:58,380 --> 00:22:00,840
a body of earth, and a tail of water.

369
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,979
I'm guessing it'll break
out of the ice pretty soon.

370
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:07,972
Do you know what that means, Miss Claire?

371
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:14,600
You and I are about to undertake our
first Herculean labor of love. Ha ha!

372
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:27,640
Oh

373
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:03,000
Thank you.

374
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,577
I can do it right now.

375
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:26,737
But it's always the same
when you're together.

376
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:29,600
It's not a bad thing.

377
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:44,800
I can't see myself.

378
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:56,357
I see you're feeling relaxed
enough to make jokes.

379
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:59,840
Yes, as long as I have you,
nothing can scare me. Good.

380
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:01,298
Then let's do this.
